<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Take Me Out to the Ball Game (Norworth's second version)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1927</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Take Me Out to the Ball Game (film, MGM, Busby Berkeley)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1949</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung by Gene Kelly and Frank Sinatra; a film named after it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A Night at the Opera (film)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1935</span><span class="sg-chain-h">its sheet music slipped to an opera orchestra by Harpo and Chico Marx</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Who's on First? (Abbott and Costello)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">sung at the start of the sketch</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Take Me Out of the Bathtub (Alan Katz and David Catrow)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2001</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody with new words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Riot at the Bat Rack (Dry Kill Logic)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2002</span><span class="sg-chain-h">loosely based on it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Take Me Out to the Ballgame (Jim Burke)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2006</span><span class="sg-chain-h">children's book</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Baseball's Greatest Hit (Andy Strasberg, Bob Thompson and Tim Wiles)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2008</span><span class="sg-chain-h">a history of the song</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Lifting the Curse (Julian Wachner and Bill Littlefield)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">quoted in, for narrator and orchestra</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Namboku Line departure melody at Kōrakuen Station</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2015</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Hartford Yard Goats' nut-free line</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2019</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words for one line</span></li></ul></section>
